          "showLineNumbers": false,
          "showMiniMap": false
        },
        "content": "### Query controls\n- **Cluster** and **Component** select indexed Loki labels. Both support multi-select and **All**.\n- **Level** performs a case-insensitive line filter so it also works for services that do not emit structured `level` labels.\n- **Search (regex)** filters message text. Use `.*` to match everything.\n- **Extra LogQL pipeline** accepts optional pipeline stages, for example `|= \"worker\"`, `| json`, or `| logfmt | duration > 1s`.\n- Use the time picker in the top-right to scroll back through retained logs. Open the logs panel menu and choose **Explore** to edit the complete LogQL query interactively.",
        "mode": "markdown"
      },
      "pluginVersion": "12.0.0",
      "title": "How to query logs",
      "type": "text"
    },
